00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:04.389
I'm gonna go ahead and
start with Dr. Jordan.

00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:06.830
Dr. Ayana Jordan is an
addiction psychiatrist

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:11.690
and the Barbara Wilson Associate
Professor in of Psychiatry

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.050
in the Department of Psychiatry

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.720
at the NYU Grossman School of Medicine.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.690
She is also the pillar lead
for the community engagement

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:23.290
in the NYU Langone Institute
of Excellence in Health Equity.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.040
Dr. Jordan is someone who is
dedicated to creating spaces

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.990
and opportunities for
more people of color,

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.420
specifically black women in academia

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.925
who are vastly underrepresented.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.540
Dr. Jordan is someone who
has a lot of accolades

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.890
and has been involved in a lot

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.400
of different pioneering
things over the years.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.894
I'm just gonna highlight a few of them,

00:01:39.894 --> 00:01:42.746
want to mention that she was
the first black associate

00:01:42.746 --> 00:01:45.070
program director for the Yale University

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.040
of Psychiatry Residency
program when she was

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.028
on faculty at Yale for quite a while.

00:01:49.028 --> 00:01:51.421
She recently also became
the Director of Equity,

00:01:51.421 --> 00:01:53.090
Diversity and Inclusion

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.989
for the Justice Community
Opioid Innovation Network.

00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:58.070
She also serves as the medical director

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.100
for the Recognizing and
Eliminating disparities

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.470
of an Addiction through
Culturally informed Healthcare

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.430
or REACH.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.270
These are funded programs
that she has garnered.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.330
So that's something that we
don't take for granted at all.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.232
She's also an NIH funded researcher

00:02:10.232 --> 00:02:12.277
where she studies the long term outcomes

00:02:12.277 --> 00:02:15.170
for providing addiction
treatment in face settings.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.007
Something that we're going
to dig into today as well.

00:02:18.007 --> 00:02:19.920
And just to wrap up and say,

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.512
she's someone who's deeply
grateful to be taking care

00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:25.916
of the most historically excluded
patients during this time

00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.230
who are facing extreme challenges

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.180
in obtaining addiction treatment,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.980
even as we continue to
walk through the pandemic.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.810
So someone who again is a pioneer

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.993
and I'm just honored to
be able to welcome her

00:02:36.993 --> 00:02:40.180
to the program and to
introduce you all as listeners

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.670
to the wonderful, talented,
inspiring and wise,

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.993
Dr. Ayana Jordan.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:49.290
- Hey me, listen, have me back anytime.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.720
I'm like, that was an amazing intro!

00:02:52.937 --> 00:02:55.250
I just wanna walk away now, but thank you.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.490
Thank you.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.640
Asha, brother, so much love.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.790
Thank you.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.090
- Yeah, definitely appreciate you.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.210
To also introduce Dr. Sidney Hankerson.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.840
Dr. Hankerson is the Director

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.580
of Mental Health Equity Research

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.030
at Mount Sinai in the Institute
for Health Equity Research.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:14.107
He is someone who has also
garnered many different grants.

00:03:14.107 --> 00:03:16.510
He's been awarded grants
from National Institute

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.232
of Mental Health, the Brain
and Behavior Foundation,

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.400
and the New York State
Office of Mental Health.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.190
He was formerly at Columbia University,

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.400
had funding through there as well,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.610
and has also been involved
in many funding sources

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.778
from private foundations.

00:03:28.778 --> 00:03:31.610
He's someone who was presented
in lots of different venues,

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.840
including the White House,

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:33.995
including the United Nations,

00:03:33.995 --> 00:03:37.040
at the National Institute
of Mental Health.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.150
Also the Substance Abuse

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.000
and Mental Health Services Administration.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.700
Also at Gracie Mansion,

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.745
also known as the New
York City mayor's office,

00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:45.840
has just been involved in the community

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.180
in so many different ways over the years.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.430
He was also an inaugural member

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.540
